## Validation and known limits

The completed local implementation passed `npm test` and `npm run build` (including TypeScript) before the handoff. Checks covered inclusive recurrence, independent completion, end-time boundary, all weekdays, timezones/DST, invalid data, exact supplied URLs and later/year-boundary dates, shared metadata/colours/tags, legacy migration, restart persistence, revision conflicts, host/origin restrictions, oversized/invalid saves, backup downloads, and private-file access. Server tests create temporary databases. The Host-header test uses Node HTTP requests because Node fetch did not preserve the supplied Host header.

These results describe the previous implementation run. Re-run appropriate checks after relevant changes; avoid running the app or destructive QA against personal data unnecessarily. For documentation-only updates, review content and `git diff --check`; a new application build/test run is not needed.

Current lifecycle validation: `npm test` passed the model checks and all nine API/launcher tests; `npm run build` passed TypeScript and production bundling. New tests cover background/foreground startup, restart persistence, repeat/concurrent opens, occupied preferred ports, exact-port environment override, invalid settings, abandoned locks, stale state/unrelated-server protection, unauthenticated/cross-site shutdown rejection, Ctrl+C, shortcut validation, mocked dialog save/cancel flows and bounded shutdown for unfinished requests. Shell syntax checks and `git diff --check` passed. Generated shortcuts were installed, executable and validated with `desktop-file-validate`. Native dialogs and default-browser opening were not visually reviewed; browser launch was suppressed in automated tests. Local bind tests required execution outside the network-restricted sandbox. The interrupted initial sandbox test attempt was not counted as passing; the successful full run used temporary databases/settings/runtime state.

Known scope: user-launched local server with desktop controls; single local planner; same-day weekly sessions; fixed materials path `2627`; recording links open filtered lists. No login-time server startup, multi-device synchronisation, holiday exceptions, or direct recording-video lookup was implemented. Desktop dialogs require `zenity` and a graphical Linux session. Moving the repository requires reinstalling its shortcuts. Existing unmanaged servers from the historical copy must be stopped separately; controls intentionally do not stop them. These are scope notes, not authorised new tasks.

